.* QSUHLP: the help of the Source Entry Utility's display files (QSUSEU,
.* QSUDFT, QSUFND, QSUBRW, QSUEXIT, QSUSYS, QSUSEL in ui/dspf/sys/).
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:HELP NAME=SEUEDIT.Source Entry Utility
:P.The edit display shows the records of a source member, one per line,
with the sequence number at the left. Type over a record to change it.
:P.On the SEU command line (SEU==>) you can type commands such as
FIND, CHANGE, TOP, BOTTOM, SAVE and FILE. In the sequence number area
you can type line commands: I to insert, D to delete, C and M to copy
and move with A or B as the target, R to repeat, P to prompt the
record, and others.
:P.F3 leaves SEU through the Exit display; F4 prompts the record the
cursor is on; F5 refreshes; F10 moves the cursor to the top line; F11
moves between the two halves of a wide record; F13 changes the session
defaults; F14 and F16 find and change; F15 browses or copies another
member, spooled file or output queue; F21 runs a system command; F24
shows the other keys.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUPROMPT.Prompt
:P.The prompt shows the fields of the record the cursor was on, laid
out by the prompt type of the member's source type. Type the values
and press Enter to put them back in the record; F12 leaves the record
as it was.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUDFT.Change Session Defaults
:P.The defaults of this editing session: how far the page keys move,
whether lower case stays as typed, the tab stops, the increment of
inserted records, whether full screen mode is on, the syntax checking
of added and changed records, and the date that marks changed records.
Press Enter to use the values for the rest of the session.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUFIND.Find/Change Options
:P.The string to find and the string to change it to, the columns to
search, which occurrences to process, which records to search and
whether case matters. F14 finds the next occurrence; F16 repeats the
last find; F17 changes the occurrence found.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUBROWSE.Browse/Copy Options
:P.Selection 1 shows another source member in the lower part of the
display; 2 shows a spooled file; 3 shows an output queue's spooled
files to choose from. With copy all records Y, the member's records
are copied into the member being edited, after the cursor's record.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUEXIT.Exit
:P.Choose how the session ends. Change/create member Y saves the
records to the member named, which can be another member, file or
library; resequence Y numbers the records from Start by Increment.
Print member Y prints the member. Return to editing Y goes back to the
edit display. Press Enter to leave with these choices; F12 returns to
editing.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUSYS.System Command
:P.Type a command and press Enter to run it without leaving SEU. F4
prompts it; F9 retrieves the last one; F12 returns to the member.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SEUSELECT.Select Prompt
:P.The prompts available for the record. Type the prompt type and press
Enter to prompt the record with it.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
